{"id":"458013236","kind":"article","title":"精细编码","author":"Andy Matuschak","original_authors":["Andy Matuschak"],"original_source_urls":["https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3ZTBNhJddpewTBgbKAFy2cnSMBiJRpMZWsfB"],"publisher":"Thoughts Memo","column":"认知基石 & 教育培训","date":"2022-01-16","updated":"2022-08-21","votes":20,"comment_count":2,"minutes":4,"chars":1982,"keywords":["精细编码","检索练习","测试效应","间隔重复","常青笔记"],"summary":"作者区分精细编码与提取练习：把新知识联系既有经验可能有助回忆，但相关实验显示，单靠概念图式的精细加工，未必比主动检索带来更多学习。笔记中的反向链接可促使人寻找概念关系，也可能形成精细编码；作者总结称，测试效应整体上似乎更持久、更能改善学习，但联想仍有助于理解。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/458013236","restoration":null,"toc":[{"id":"sec-1","level":2,"title":"参考文献"},{"id":"sec-2","level":2,"title":"反向链接"},{"id":"sec-3","level":2,"title":"声明"}],"html":"<p data-pid=\"OwV-ZOle\">「精细编码」描述了将知识与现有记忆或经历建立联系的过程。一般认为，建立这样的联系有助于回忆，特别是与十分独特或有情感连接的目标建立联系时。</p><p data-pid=\"71urKnit\">精细编码最常用于助记法：记忆数字时，将数字与名人、地点、气味等事物建立联系。</p><p data-pid=\"TJE8LrF_\">一些<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4eXdSMJFv2qVGXSUEKH4vdcHBrLHcFY1ZGfC\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复记忆系统</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>的用户会特意写出卡片，以促进精细编码。Karpicke 和 Smith 的实验（2012）表明，与只进行提取练习相比，这样做的好处并不大。相关文章： <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z6z7GhYwjvT6eYbBDQgUbmcshywmskqnVs3Y6\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">提取练习似乎是一种比精细编码更有效的学习活动</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>。</p><h2 id=\"sec-1\">参考文献</h2><p data-pid=\"0S-dkKBd\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z78CeJK6CpQWhzruLZZ8cVxeQ2WaHgzHNmHsq\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Karpicke, J. D., &amp; Blunt, J. R. (2011). Retrieval Practice Produces More Learning than Elaborative Studying with Concept Mapping. Science, 331(6018), 772–775.</a></p><p data-pid=\"zXHKenwl\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/Karpicke,_J._D.,_&amp;_Smith,_M._A._(2012)._Separate_mnemonic_effects_of_retrieval_practice_and_elaborative_encoding._Journal_of_Memory_and_Language,_67(1),_17–29._https\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">//doi.org/10.1016/j.jml.2012.02.004</a></p><h2 id=\"sec-2\">反向链接</h2><ul><li data-pid=\"RU1lJiIZ\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z2HUE4ABbQjUNjrNemvkTCsLa1LPDRuwh1tXC\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">常青笔记之间应该建立大量链接</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup><br/> <br/></li><ul><li data-pid=\"OF7qWZXJ\"> 强迫自己在笔记之间添加大量链接，我们便能打开视野，围绕眼下关心的问题，考虑还有些概念能与其关联。添加链接的行为施加了一种压力，促使我们仔细思考各个概念如何联系彼此（见<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zX1WtJ4ouE8sjN1NgWHsGVg8ZnVfp5Kz74Vs\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">理解概念需与其尽力较量</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-4\"><a href=\"#ref-4\">[4]</a></sup>和<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z6bci25mVUBNFdVWSrQNKr6u7AZ1jFzfTVbMF\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">常青笔记应该面向概念</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-5\"><a href=\"#ref-5\">[5]</a></sup>），同时也实现了<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3ZTBNhJddpewTBgbKAFy2cnSMBiJRpMZWsfB\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">精细编码</a>，使我们更深入地内化这些想法。<br/> <br/></li></ul><li data-pid=\"hX0wkA77\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z45mhbpabsigFceeSiRyDXZdvcRqvE2A1xMsn\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">测试效应</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-6\"><a href=\"#ref-6\">[6]</a></sup><br/> <br/></li><ul><li data-pid=\"ZqYWwF_p\"> 总体而言，与只基于<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3ZTBNhJddpewTBgbKAFy2cnSMBiJRpMZWsfB\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">精细编码</a>的练习相比，测试效应似乎还能带来更持久的记忆 (Karpicke and Smith, 2012)，并改善学习表现 (Karpicke and Blunt, 2011)。<br/> <br/></li></ul><li data-pid=\"Npq_a14K\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z78CeJK6CpQWhzruLZZ8cVxeQ2WaHgzHNmHsq\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Karpicke, J. D., &amp; Blunt, J. R. (2011). Retrieval Practice Produces More Learning than Elaborative Studying with Concept Mapping. Science, 331(6018), 772–775.</a><br/> <br/></li><ul><li data-pid=\"trBU5bq6\"> 实验比较了概念图（调用<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3ZTBNhJddpewTBgbKAFy2cnSMBiJRpMZWsfB\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">精细编码</a>）与提取练习（调用<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z45mhbpabsigFceeSiRyDXZdvcRqvE2A1xMsn\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">测试效应</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-6\"><a href=\"#ref-6\">[6]</a></sup>）对记忆的影响。与 Karpicke 和 Smith（2012）一样，本文也对提取练习的效果是否可能<b>取决于</b>精细编码，或者是否有其他过程发生感兴趣。<br/> <br/></li></ul><li data-pid=\"7rUhAcxK\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z49EwwPL1CzKHTyLHXwJJH7hsciCg772Vm5WJ\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复记忆卡片应关联和联系概念</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-7\"><a href=\"#ref-7\">[7]</a></sup><br/> <br/></li><ul><li data-pid=\"rffsuXim\">当使用<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4eXdSMJFv2qVGXSUEKH4vdcHBrLHcFY1ZGfC\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复记忆系统</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>来学习事实时，天真的方法会导致孤立地学习很多事实：一种蛋白质的名称、一个事件的日期、一个物理常数的大小。但是因为<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z8LFKKV15V11DpHdrybyvcaXcVfcRNqVqVCTD\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">丰富的理解在于联系</a>，最好是将这些事实与其他想法联系起来。这既能帮助你更可靠地记忆（由于<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3ZTBNhJddpewTBgbKAFy2cnSMBiJRpMZWsfB\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">精细编码</a>），也能帮助你形成更丰富的理解，超越简单的事实。<br/><br/></li></ul><li data-pid=\"DUhab5An\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zEfpMY7F12gQ6NcbycHCNdpXqxb2mxdkJiX\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">专家回答启发式，来自 Issa Rice</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-8\"><a href=\"#ref-8\">[8]</a></sup><br/> <br/></li><ul><li data-pid=\"ul9cedlC\">当一张卡片不能用上这种启发式方法时，它通常是在编码作者特定的解释、框架、例子、措辞等。这通常很有帮助，特别是作为一种<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3ZTBNhJddpewTBgbKAFy2cnSMBiJRpMZWsfB\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">精细编码</a>或培养情感兴趣的一种方式。但它也可能产生偏狭的理解。在使用共享卡片或助记媒介的情况下，这种卡片会产生令人沮丧的假阴性，因为它们要求读者学习卡片作者如何呈现材料：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zMFKJdtNGpucVUcitRVJiMxfyoNY4A4c2Bd\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">助记媒介的读者有时会因为作者的措辞选择而感到受阻</a>。<br/><br/></li></ul><li data-pid=\"uRhPcr1U\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z219EBYg9SbQzF372qudzgJpArt4Bmfhrczkg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">亲自写间隔重复卡片似乎能促进理解</a><br/> <br/></li><ul><li data-pid=\"bUtBbSYY\"> 相关笔记：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3iJVoXtJBUJHq9Tb6i8Kv4EK7oNbriHh4N2y\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">生成效应</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-9\"><a href=\"#ref-9\">[9]</a></sup>，<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3ZTBNhJddpewTBgbKAFy2cnSMBiJRpMZWsfB\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">精细编码</a><br/><br/> </li></ul><li data-pid=\"bgNYN671\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z8LFKKV15V11DpHdrybyvcaXcVfcRNqVqVCTD\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">丰富的理解在于联系</a><br/> <br/></li><ul><li data-pid=\"V5nX1ndq\"> 这部分内容是关于<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3ZTBNhJddpewTBgbKAFy2cnSMBiJRpMZWsfB\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">精细编码</a>。<br/> <br/></li></ul><li data-pid=\"eBuOUSUM\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z2jtKy8tjoEMhzzbgFMnf61BXYe1dkNgKrssE\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">2020-11-01 – 2020-11-07</a><br/> <br/></li><ul><li data-pid=\"sJb4FxzH\">对<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z45mhbpabsigFceeSiRyDXZdvcRqvE2A1xMsn\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">测试效应</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-6\"><a href=\"#ref-6\">[6]</a></sup>和<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3iJVoXtJBUJHq9Tb6i8Kv4EK7oNbriHh4N2y\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">生成效应</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-9\"><a href=\"#ref-9\">[9]</a></sup>有了更好的理解，围绕这个问题读了一堆论文。对<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3ZTBNhJddpewTBgbKAFy2cnSMBiJRpMZWsfB\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">精细编码</a>的理解逐渐加深。一篇不错的综述文章：<br/><br/></li></ul><li data-pid=\"btDoick1\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z42jyZFjBkbLnM5ik4J69FsADkdjNBTJjoBy7\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Active Learning Online - Stephen Kosslyn</a><br/><br/></li><ul><li data-pid=\"ohJZeUG1\">问：什么令人惊讶的实验结果说明了「深度加工」原理？<br/><br/></li></ul><li data-pid=\"U7snTrn5\"> [[Karpicke, J. D., &amp; Smith, M. A. (2012). Separate mnemonic effects of retrieval practice and elaborative encoding. Journal of Memory and Language, 67(1), 17–29. <a class=\"external\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jml.2012.02.004\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"visible\">doi.org/10.1016/j.jml.2</span><span class=\"invisible\">012.02.004</span><span class=\"ellipsis\"></span></a>]]<br/><br/>* <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z45mhbpabsigFceeSiRyDXZdvcRqvE2A1xMsn\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">测试效应</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-6\"><a href=\"#ref-6\">[6]</a></sup>是由<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3ZTBNhJddpewTBgbKAFy2cnSMBiJRpMZWsfB\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">精细编码</a>产生的吗？当你在<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4eXdSMJFv2qVGXSUEKH4vdcHBrLHcFY1ZGfC\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复记忆系统</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>中复习卡片时，你给自己一个机会，根据你当前的上下文和复习过程中产生的不同想法形成新的联系。</li></ul><h2 id=\"sec-3\">声明</h2><p data-pid=\"EXe-X8pe\">此内容发布由 Andy Matuschak 许可。未经允许，不得转载或修改。保留所有权利。</p><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><blockquote data-pid=\"ALGCT-HI\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://paratranz.cn/projects/3131\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Thoughts Memo</a> 汉化组译制<br/>原文：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3ZTBNhJddpewTBgbKAFy2cnSMBiJRpMZWsfB\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Elaborative encoding (andymatuschak.org)</a></blockquote><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> 间隔重复记忆系统 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"404257681\" href=\"#/post/404257681\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-2\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-2\">↩</a> 提取练习似乎是一种比精细编码更有效的学习活动 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"556121198\" href=\"#/post/556121198\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-3\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-3\">↩</a> 常青笔记之间应该建立大量链接 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"426450021\" href=\"#/post/426450021\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-4\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-4\">↩</a> 理解概念需与其尽力较量 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"442692019\" href=\"#/post/442692019\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-5\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-5\">↩</a> 常青笔记应面向概念 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"421580357\" href=\"#/post/421580357\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-6\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-6\">↩</a> 测试效应 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"423449068\" href=\"#/post/423449068\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-7\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-7\">↩</a> 间隔重复记忆卡片应关联和联系概念 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"405151942\" href=\"#/post/405151942\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-8\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-8\">↩</a> 在 Issa Rice 之后，专家回答启发式 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"404586617\" href=\"#/post/404586617\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-9\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-9\">↩</a> 生成效应 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"455748242\" href=\"#/post/455748242\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li></ol>","rec_chain":[{"id":"457666825","title":"认知脚手架","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":32,"minutes":2,"reason":"同专栏上一篇 · 认知基石 & 教育培训"},{"id":"458799119","title":"文本的叙述作为认知脚手架","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":10,"minutes":1,"reason":"同专栏下一篇 · 认知基石 & 教育培训"},{"id":"404586617","title":"专家回答启发式（来自 Issa Rice）","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":12,"minutes":1,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"650014568","title":"助记媒介的读者有时会因作者的用词而感到受阻","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":5,"minutes":4,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"426450021","title":"常青笔记之间应该建立大量链接","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":27,"minutes":4,"reason":"本文直接引用"}],"rec_bridge":[],"rec_answers":[{"id":"1966193463411319610","title":"思维导图真的能提高学习效率和创造力吗，它的局限性在哪里？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":94,"minutes":8,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 94 赞同","evidence":"正文脚注或准确链接卡标题明确指向该译文/研究条目。"},{"id":"2834169225","title":"如何学会正确的理解记忆？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":32,"minutes":7,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 32 赞同","evidence":"回答含指向该译文的原生引用锚点，可唯一定位到该标题/关键词。"},{"id":"2772990761","title":"如何构建自己的笔记系统？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":755,"minutes":20,"reason":"延伸提及 · 755 赞同","evidence":"回答正文连续重现目标译文的特异内容，且译文侧对应段落可逐字核验。"},{"id":"1955202241058301369","title":"认知科学如何帮助我更高效地学习和记忆？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":399,"minutes":15,"reason":"延伸提及 · 399 赞同","evidence":"正文连续摘录目标译文正文；两侧对应原句可核验，计 3 级。"}]}